# Cloudflare Pages redirects for DetectLab.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This file is intentionally EMPTY of rules, and that is the correct state.
# It is the Cloudflare twin of the two [[redirects]] hostname rules in
# netlify.toml — but Cloudflare Pages cannot express them here.
#
# netlify.toml (untouched, still live):
#   from = "https://www.detectlab.eu/*"  to = "https://detectlab.eu/:splat"  status = 301 force = true
#   from = "https://www.detectlab.ro/*"  to = "https://detectlab.ro/:splat"  status = 301 force = true
#
# 1. HOSTNAME RULES ARE NOT SUPPORTED BY PAGES `_redirects`
#    The Pages redirects documentation lists "Domain-level redirects ❌"
#    (example given: `workers.example.com/* workers.example.com/blog/:splat 301`).
#    A `_redirects` source is a path, never a host, so `www.detectlab.ro/*`
#    cannot be matched here. The two canonicalisations are therefore implemented
#    in two places instead, and BOTH are required:
#
#      a) functions/_middleware.js — a 301 from www.detectlab.ro/.eu to its own
#         apex, preserving path and query. It runs for every request that
#         reaches Pages Functions, i.e. the nine /api/… paths listed in
#         cloudflare/_routes.json.
#
#      b) A Cloudflare Redirect Rule (or Bulk Redirect list) — MANUAL, in the
#         Dashboard, because it is the only mechanism that also covers static
#         asset requests, which `_routes.json` deliberately keeps away from
#         Functions. Exact expressions, one rule per zone, in
#         CLOUDFLARE_MIGRATION.md §6.4 and CLOUDFLARE_DASHBOARD_CHECKLIST.md.
#
# 2. THE TWO COUNTRY DOMAINS MUST NEVER REDIRECT TO EACH OTHER
#    detectlab.ro is the Romanian market and detectlab.eu the European one; they
#    share one deployment and one account database, but a .ro request must never
#    be answered from .eu or vice versa (DOMAIN_SETUP.md, and js/site-config.js
#    derives the market, the default language and the contact address from the
#    hostname). Consequently there is ONE rule per zone, each matching only its
#    own `www` host, and no rule may use a wildcard host or a shared list that
#    spans both zones. functions/_middleware.js encodes the same invariant as an
#    explicit host → apex table, and test-cloudflare-config.mjs asserts that the
#    table contains no cross-market pair.
#
# 3. THE NINE API ROUTES NEED NO REDIRECT HERE
#    netlify.toml reaches its functions with `status = 200` rewrites
#    (/api/geo/dk-dhm → /.netlify/functions/dk-dhm). Cloudflare Pages does not
#    need an equivalent: functions/ uses filesystem routing, so
#    functions/api/geo/dk-dhm.js already IS /api/geo/dk-dhm. Pages `_redirects`
#    proxying only supports relative URLs on the same site anyway, and adding a
#    catch-all here would risk shadowing the PWA assets, the map tiles and the
#    application paths — which the migration brief forbids.
#
# 4. NOTHING ELSE IS REDIRECTED
#    No catch-all, no trailing-slash normalisation, no extension stripping.
#    Every path that resolves on Netlify resolves identically here.
